::  name       frame max lines
::  shape      max - int (@u32)
::  invariant  Tally-bounded Frame ceiling; seed and wayland_seed both use 8
::  example    8
::  readers    Brushstroke - Surface - connector hop 3
::  nib        surface-p15-v0
::
::  Surface Chapter p15 -- second pedestal in src/sur (structure museum).
::  The published ceiling is brushstroke/brush_parse.rye max_frame_lines, and
::  the same eight is written again as a private max_lines in
::  brushstroke/seed.rye and brushstroke/wayland_seed.rye, each asserting
::  against its own copy. Four sites, one number, held together by
::  tools/s/shape_constant_pedestal_witness.rish rather than by care.
::  Does not invent a second Frame type.
+$  frame-max-lines-shape
  $:  max=@u32
  ==
